  "term": "checklist",
  "definition": "In assessment, a checklist is a structured screening tool made up of specific items that are scored to capture important behavior patterns or symptoms. In the supplied source, it refers to an observation-based scale with multiple items across key developmental domains, used to help identify young children who are more or less likely to have autism.",
