      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "The definition makes a general, field-wide claim: “In assessment, a checklist is a structured screening tool…scored to capture important behavior patterns or symptoms.” The packet only describes a specific instrument (“Checklist for Chinese Toddlers with Autism”) and does not support this general definition of “checklist” in assessment broadly.",
        "The packet does support that the particular tool is an early, culturally adapted screening measure for autism spectrum disorder, uses behavioral observation, and consists of multiple items across three dimensions (social behaviors/communication and interest behaviors & sensory perception), but the initial general characterization of “checklist” as a general assessment instrument is not supported by the packet."
